 "text": "Departments | Wichita County, KS\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nDepartments\nVisitors\nSearch\nAppraiser\n2026 Market Study (PDF)\nPersonal Property\nReal Estate\nResources\nCemetery Sexton\nCounty Clerk\nBudgets\nTax Levies\nAdditional Duties\nCounty Commissioners\nElections\nUNOFFICIAL Election Results\nLegal Publications\nOfficial Election Results\nSample Ballot\nAffidavit of Write-in (PDF)\nVoters Rights and Responsibilities (PDF)\nVoter Instructions (PDF)\nForms & Permits\nFreedom of Information\n2026 Rural Fire Budget Hearing (PDF)\n2026 Cemetery Budget Hearing (PDF)\nCounty Commissioners\nRegister of Deeds\nFee Schedule\nLinks & Forms\nText My Gov\nText My Gov Alerts (PDF)\nTreasurer\nDriver's License\nResources\nTax\nTax Calendar\nTax Payment Online\nTax Search\nVehicle Registration\nHome\nDepartments\nDepartments\n9\n1\n1\n2\nAppraiser\nmaintains maps of the county, ownership and valuation records of each property in the county.\nCemetery Sexton\nresponsible for the upkeep and management of a cemetery\nCounty Clerk\nThe Wichita County County Clerk webpage provides official information on elections, budgets, freedom-of-information requests, tax levies, payroll and benefits, cereal malt beverage licensing, and state park licensing for residents of Wichita County, Kansas.\nCounty Commissioners\nInformation on Wichita County’s three-member Board of Commissioners, including roles, contacts, meeting schedule, and agenda request procedures.\nRegister of Deeds\nOverview of the Wichita County Register of Deeds Office, including services for recording and preserving property records, fees, and contact information.\nText My Gov\nA convenient text messaging service that allows residents to access city or county information, report issues, and receive important updates directly on their mobile phones. Simply text keywords to the designated number to connect with local services anytime.\nTreasurer\nThe Treasurer’s Office manages the collection of property taxes, motor vehicle registration, and other county revenues. This section provides information on payment options, deadlines, and services offered to residents and businesses.\nAppraiser\nCounty Clerk\nElections\nRegister of Deeds\nTreasurer\nPay Taxes\nWichita County\nCounty Offices\n206 South 4th Street\nLeoti, Kansas 67861\nCounty Commissioners\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nHome\nContact Us\nAccessibility\nSite Map\nCopyright Notices\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by CivicPlus®\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nClose ×",
